ts go through the CLI. The `startsWith` plus separator check is the same thing as a lookahead. Drop the `export`s at minimum.\n   - **Size:** about 6 lines, small.\n\n4. **`lint-command` (the `if (an)` block): split the per-group checks into their own loop.**\n   - **Change:** Move the `mechanical-on-floor` and `test-serves-nothing` checks out of the `if (an)` block. `unknown-serves` and `required-but-nothing-breaks` already sit in a separate `for (const g of a.groups)` loop, and these two could share it, with `f` fetched via `an?.groups.get`.\n   - **Why:** There is one per-group pass instead of two, and `an` is checked in one place.\n   - **Size:** small. This one is mostly taste.\n\nThe change is otherwise lean. Reusing `ratingIssues` instead of copying the rules is the right call, and the tests cover each code.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
