n findings (`src/commands/lint.ts`, the `clean` mapping).** Findings are built from raw strings and sanitized in one pass at the end. Sanitizing at construction would let the `clean` mapping and the `f.group !== undefined` branches go away. This is a minor cleanup and changes little.\n\n5. **Text output grouping (`src/commands/lint.ts`, the `subjects` Map).** The Map plus the key ternary could be a sort on a `subject` string computed once per finding. Low benefit.\n\nThe diff is otherwise lean. The `ratingIssues` split is the right shape, and the lint command reuses it rather than duplicating the floor rules. The main cleanup opportunities are items 1 and 2.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
